Day 18 — Lists & Keys

Imagine an e-commerce website with 100 products.

You definitely don't want to write:

<p>Groundnut Oil</p>
<p>Coconut Oil</p>
<p>Sunflower Oil</p>
<p>Sesame Oil</p>
<p>Mustard Oil</p>

Instead, you normally receive an array of data:

const products = [
  "Groundnut Oil",
  "Coconut Oil",
  "Sunflower Oil",
  "Sesame Oil",
];

React can automatically turn this data into UI.



3. Real-World Analogy

Imagine a restaurant has an order list:

Burger
Pizza
